<title>UK: ICI says pound may hit 1997 profits.</title>
<headline>ICI says pound may hit 1997 profits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Chemical Industries Plc said on Thursday that if sterling stayed at current high levels, &quot;the effect on this year compared with 1996 as a whole could be in the 80 million to 90 million stg range&quot;.</p>
<p>Finance Director Alan Spall told a post-results news conference that a surge in sterling in the last quarter of 1996 had offset a 15 million stg currency gain reported at the nine month stage.</p>
<p>He added that exchange effects on profits in 1996 as a whole were negligible.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
